593971,0.0,0.0,-0.8319458961486816,-1.5067241191864014,0.0,-0.7805027961730957,-0.026898376643657684,-0.00034505134681239724,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,0.0,-4.768370445162873e-07,0.0,-3.2186455882765586e-06,0.0,-1.311301275563892e-06,-3.4570634852570947e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,82345,279,1985,1124,9697,59,26888,220,20,41715,26888,21,41715,26888,22,2376,30529,26888,220,20,41715,26888,21,41715,26888,22,2376,59,26888,220,20,30529,26888,21,41715,26888,22,2376,59,26888,220,20,41715,26888,21,30529,26888,22,72341,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nEvaluate the product \\[(\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(-\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt 5-\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6-\\sqrt7).\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"240045541b2fddda62a12db78181306ce3644a8bff4d96c2e19fcc74ebf36670"},"seconds":39.69314885139465,"seed":543176259418523195,"stop":"eos","text":"To evaluate the product \\[(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{7})(-\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{7}),\\] we can use a substitution to simplify the expression.\n\nLet's denote:\n\\[ a = \\sqrt{5}, \\]\n\\[ b = \\sqrt{6}, \\]\n\\[ c = \\sqrt{7}. \\]\n\nThen the expression becomes:\n\\[ (a+b+c)(-a+b+c)(a-b+c)(a+b-c). \\]\n\nWe can group the terms in pairs and use the difference of squares formula:\n\\[ [(a+b+c)(-a+b+c)][(a-b+c)(a+b-c)]. \\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify \\((a+b+c)(-a+b+c)\\):\n\\[\n(a+b+c)(-a+b+c) = [(b+c)+a][(b+c)-a] = (b+c)^2 - a^2.\n\\]\nSince \\( a = \\sqrt{5} \\), \\( b = \\sqrt{6} \\), and \\( c = \\sqrt{7} \\), we have:\n\\[\n(b+c)^2 - a^2 = (\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{7})^2 - (\\sqrt{5})^2 = (6 + 2\\sqrt{42} + 7) - 5 = 8 + 2\\sqrt{42}.\n\\]\n\nNext, let's simplify \\((a-b+c)(a+b-c)\\):\n\\[\n(a-b+c)(a+b-c) = [a+(c-b)][a-(c-b)] = a^2 - (c-b)^2.\n\\]\nSince \\( a = \\sqrt{5} \\), \\( b = \\sqrt{6} \\), and \\( c = \\sqrt{7} \\), we have:\n\\[\na^2 - (c-b)^2 = (\\sqrt{5})^2 - (\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{6})^2 = 5 - (7 - 2\\sqrt{42} + 6) = 5 - (13 - 2\\sqrt{42}) = 5 - 13 + 2\\sqrt{42} = -8 + 2\\sqrt{42}.\n\\]\n\nNow we multiply the two results:\n\\[\n(8 + 2\\sqrt{42})(-8 + 2\\sqrt{42}).\n\\]\nThis is another difference of squares:\n\\[\n(8 + 2\\sqrt{42})(-8 + 2\\sqrt{42}) = (2\\sqrt{42})^2 - 8^2 = 4 \\cdot 42 - 64 = 168 - 64 = 104.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the original product is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{104}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{104}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
